rustc_codegen_js: mark FromStr for host dec2flt and delegate f32/f64 Formatter float formatting.

Mark `core::str::FromStr` with a private compiler-owned diagnostic item so the
backend recognizes `<f64 as FromStr>::from_str` and `<f32 as FromStr>::from_str`
by exact rustc identity (never by path/symbol substrings), allowing `jsc-link`
to replace their bodies with host-delegated IEEE-754 parsing and drop `dec2flt`.

Delegate `f32` and `f64` `Display`/`Debug`/`LowerExp`/`UpperExp` formatting in
`core::fmt::float` to `rcgjs_fmt_float_parts` feeding `Formatter::pad_formatted_parts`,
preserving 100% of `Formatter` width/alignment/fill/zero-pad/error semantics
while dropping `core::num::imp::flt2dec` (Grisu/Dragon4/BigNum).

